    <h2>Method 1 — Check the page footer</h2>
    <p>The footer is the first place to look because many agencies and platform builders include their branding there by default, either as a legal attribution or as a free advertising trade-off baked into their pricing model.</p>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1</span>
      <h3>Scroll to the very bottom of any page</h3>
      <p>Look for text such as "Designed by Studio X", "Built with Webflow", "Powered by Squarespace", "Shopify — E-commerce by <em>Theme Name</em>", or a small agency logo with a link.</p>
      <p>Free tiers of website builders (Wix, Weebly, Webflow Starter) almost always add a branded footer badge — this immediately tells you both the platform and the fact that the owner is on a free plan.</p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Limitation:</strong> Paid plans and custom builds routinely strip footer attribution, so the absence of a credit does not mean there is nothing to find.</p>
  </section>

